id: pm-web-2rek
title: Cross-process real-time bus so pm-gpt/pm-mcp edits reach pm-web SSE clients (and scale across replicas)
description: "FINDING (2026-07-11 hosted-services audit): pm-web already has SSE real-time (services/sse.ts: broadcastProjectEvent + presence), but the client registry is an in-memory per-process array (clients: SSEClient[]). There is NO cross-process propagation (no LISTEN/NOTIFY, Redis, or fs.watch). Consequences for the hosted stack (pm-web + pm-gpt + pm-mcp all share the pm-cli_pm-web-projects volume + Postgres): (1) an edit made via ChatGPT/pm-gpt writes the shared volume directly and does NOT trigger a pm-web SSE broadcast, so pm-web UI users only see it on manual refresh; (2) horizontally scaling pm-web to serve thousands of concurrent users breaks live updates because SSE clients on replica A never receive events broadcast on replica B. Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY is the natural fix (shared dep, no new infra). This is the gap between 'has real-time' and 'multi-user real-time live collaboration across all connected services'."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-11T15:54:35.079Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T05:05:46.089Z"
assignee: claude-orchestrator
author: claude
acceptance_criteria: "SSE broadcasts propagate across processes/replicas via Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY (Postgres is already a shared dependency — no new infra). On any pm item create/update/close — whether made by pm-web itself, pm-gpt (ChatGPT), or pm-mcp writing to the shared PROJECTS_ROOT volume — a NOTIFY is emitted; every pm-web instance LISTENs and re-broadcasts to its local SSE clients (item events + presence). Writes that bypass the pm-web API (direct file writes on the shared volume) are still surfaced (via a NOTIFY hook or a lightweight change-detector). Verified: an edit via pm-gpt appears in a pm-web UI SSE stream in real time; two pm-web instances sharing the DB both deliver the same event. No data loss; no regression to single-process behavior."
actual_result: "Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY propagation, project-indexed SSE fan-out, reconnect handling, pm-gpt publishing, and 2000-client production capacity are implemented and verified. Remaining acceptance scope: arbitrary direct-file change detection and explicit two-pm-web-replica delivery test."
notes[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-12T15:04:26.232Z",codex,"Second pre-push Greptile 95372384 found the dedicated LISTEN client lacked an error handler. The bus now consumes client errors, destroys the failed connection, reconnects with capped exponential backoff, resets after recovery, and shuts down without reconnecting. Full gate passes with 68 tests and Docker image sha256:512210671a02."
  "2026-07-12T15:39:51.156Z",codex,"GitHub review follow-up: oversized NOTIFY payloads now emit a safe warning, the pool defaults to 20 connections including the dedicated listener, SSE display-name lookup completes before headers, and the runtime container has a healthcheck plus non-root default. Hosted compose already overrides UID/GID 10001:10001 to match its persistent bind mount."
  "2026-07-12T16:26:40.170Z",codex,"2026-07-12 final pre-push review correction: a listener connection that completes after shutdown now explicitly UNLISTENs before returning to the pool, preventing a reused pooled connection from retaining the channel subscription. Runtime startup errors now use an accurate component-neutral diagnostic."
  "2026-07-12T17:32:24.370Z",codex,"2026-07-12 production milestone: public PR #39 merged/deployed. Fresh hosted run connected 2000/2000, cross-process pg_notify delivered 2000/2000 in 199 ms max, 0 drops over 65 seconds, and post-soak fan-out delivered 2000/2000 in 915 ms max. Keep feature open for direct-file watcher and explicit multi-replica test."
  "2026-07-23T20:15:19.427Z",claude-orchestrator,"Implementing the two remaining acceptance items on branch feat/external-change-detector-realtime. (1) LIGHTWEIGHT CHANGE-DETECTOR for out-of-band direct writes to the shared PROJECTS_ROOT volume: polls ONLY projects that currently have SSE clients (scales with live viewership, avoids inotify/node_modules watch explosion; extensions/pm-graph/node_modules has ~2700 files per project). Maps projectId->dir via cached DB lookup (pm_projects.id -> user_id+slug -> PROJECTS_ROOT/<userId>/<slug>), scans item .toon + history .jsonl mtimes (excludes extensions/runtime/locks/search/index), emits local 'workspace-changed' (client already refreshes on it, silent — no userId => no toast). SUPPRESSES changes already signaled via deliverProjectEvent (pm-web API writes + pm-gpt NOTIFYs both flow through it) using a wall-clock window > poll interval, so no doubling of SSE traffic at scale. (2) TWO-REPLICA DELIVERY TEST: minimal realtime-bus refactor exporting pure buildEnvelope/handleIncomingEnvelope so a test proves a message published by replica A is delivered by replica B and self-skipped by A — infra-free (CI has no Postgres). Confirmed: pm-gpt==pm-mcp writes directly + pg_notify (workspaces.ts:123); hosted pm-web built from public ./fleet/pm-web via companion compose."
  "2026-07-23T20:37:47.977Z",claude-orchestrator,"IMPLEMENTED + VERIFIED (branch feat/external-change-detector-realtime). Files: src/services/project-watcher.ts (new lightweight change-detector), src/services/sse.ts (noteSignaledMutation/wasSignaledWithin/getActiveProjectIds + deliverProjectEvent suppression hook + TTL prune), src/services/realtime-bus.ts (extracted pure buildEnvelope/handleIncomingEnvelope, reconnect logic untouched), src/server.ts (wired startProjectWatcher + stop-on-close), src/services/pm-runner.ts (export projectsRoot). Tests: test/project-watcher.test.ts (6 cases), test/realtime-bus.test.ts (5 cases incl. genuine two-replica A->B deliver / A self-skip). Implementation by pi (glm-5.2). VERIFICATION (claude-orchestrator): typecheck OK; build OK; canonical npm test 117/117 pass; audit:prod 0 vulns; pack:dry-run 217 files; changelog:check up-to-date; production smoke (built dist) start/stop clean; REAL-FILESYSTEM functional test PASS (detects .toon + history/.jsonl edits, ignores extensions/node_modules + runtime, honors suppression, baseline-no-emit). NOTE: local-only fs hang earlier was a STALE gitignored dist-test/seo-routes.test.js artifact with no source (never in CI) + flaky host DNS — removed; unrelated to this change."
  "2026-07-24T05:05:46.088Z",claude-orchestrator,"Bot-review hardening round (PR #56, CodeRabbit + Sourcery):\n- CodeRabbit Major (project-watcher.ts): a reduced max(mtime) missed mtime-preserving restores (files rewritten with OLDER preserved mtimes never advance the max) and same-instant add/remove. Replaced with a composite signature `count:max:sum(mtime BigInt)` computed in the same stat pass (zero extra I/O); emit switched from emit-on-increase to emit-on-change. Real-filesystem functional test confirms an older-mtime restore is now detected while extensions/node_modules churn stays ignored. The >8000-file cap remains a documented backstop (bounded round-robin scan tracked as follow-up).\n- CodeRabbit + Sourcery (both flagged): defaultResolveProjectDir swallowed transient DB errors and cached null for the whole SSE session, permanently silencing the watcher for that project. Now DB errors propagate to onError (retried next tick); only genuine misses/successes are cached. New unit test proves throw-then-retry.\n- Sourcery test suggestions: added realtime-bus tests for non-plain-object data normalizing to {} and whitelist/length bounding (which is WHY buildEnvelope can never approach the 7.5KB cap — the oversized-through-buildEnvelope path is unreachable by construction).\nVerified: typecheck + build clean, 121/121 tests (was 117), audit:prod 0 vulns, changelog:check up to date."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  src/services/realtime-bus.ts,project,PostgreSQL LISTEN/NOTIFY transport
  src/services/sse.ts,project,Per-project local fan-out and presence
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,note}:
  npm test,project,600,Realtime reconnect and isolation tests
